Article 3 (Definitions) The terms used in these Rules are defined as follows:
1. "VIP lounge" means a place specially installed in an airport terminal to extend courtesies to distinguished guests prescribed by these Rules when they enter or leave the country;
2. "Proxy handling of immigration procedures" means carrying out immigration procedures on behalf of a distinguished guest entering or leaving the country;
3. "Proxy handler of immigration procedures" means an airport protocol officer or a person entrusted by a distinguished guest to handle immigration procedures on his or her behalf;
4. "Immigration inspection area" means an immigration examination area, bonded area, quarantine area, and other areas specially designated at an airport where international aircraft arrive or depart in order to perform immigration control, customs clearance, quarantine, and similar functions as prescribed by statutes.
